#~
Fuzzer finding against v2026.9.4 (x64 Windows). The fuzzer's reduction of
seed 1015 stopped at 142 lines (a 1500-test budget); this is the construct it
kept, written by hand.

signature: crash: s3/jit1 access violation; diverge: s0/off,s3/off,s3/default | s3/jit1,s0/jit1 first=h=# vs

A zero-argument lambda that returns a basic type, `\() ~ Int : () => e`,
compiles, and calling it works in the interpreter (h=6). With --jit=1, at s0
or s3, obr dies with an access violation (0xC0000005) and prints nothing. The
default threshold passes here only because Main holds no loop and is never
compiled; inside a method called ten times it crashes the same way.

tools/fuzz/gen.py generates this form only with --basic-lambdas: a native
crash carries no message, so no known.json regex could tell it apart from a
new JIT crash.

Expected output: h=6
~#

class Lam3 {
  function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
    x := 5;
    h := \() ~ Int : () => x + 1;
    hr := h();
    "h={$hr}"->PrintLine();
  }
}
